  "plan": "1. Explore the environment: check user, OS, and availability of git, sshd, python3, openssl, curl. 2. Install missing packages if needed. 3. Set up SSH (sshd, user 'user', key auth, /etc/hosts entry for 'server'). 4. Create bare repo /git/server with a post-receive hook that deploys pushed branches to /var/www/html via git archive. 5. Generate a trusted self-signed cert and run an HTTPS server on 8080 serving /var/www/html. 6. Test the full flow with a clone/push and curl.",
  "commands": [
    {"keystrokes": "id; cat /etc/os-release | head -3\n", "duration": 0.1},
